---
description: React Three Fiber architecture rules
alwaysApply: true
---

React Three Fiber code must be performance-conscious.

Rules:
- Do not call React setState inside useFrame.
- Use refs and lerp for per-frame animation.
- Keep topology data-driven from runtimeConfig.ts.
- Keep labels readable and accessible.
- Keep Canvas DPR capped at [1, 1.5].
- Use Suspense/lazy loading for heavy scene code.
- Provide reduced-motion and mobile fallback.
- Do not mount/unmount expensive 3D objects repeatedly for simple state changes.
- Keep scene components small and named clearly.

Preferred scene architecture:

RuntimeSceneImpl
├── BlenderEnvironment or ProceduralEnvironment
├── RuntimeCore
├── RuntimeNodeBlock
├── DataLink
├── DataPacket
├── CameraRig
└── SceneLabels
